     <p>There are more puzzle sites than anyone can play in a lifetime, and they are not all equal. Here are five worth your time, with an honest word about each, including our own.</p>
 
     <h3>1. GridPaw</h3>
-    <p>That is us, and since honesty was promised: GridPaw focuses on Japanese-style grid puzzles rather than trying to host every puzzle ever invented. Shikaku and Akari are the flagship pair, and the catalog has grown around them — Kakuro, Nonogram, Nurikabe, KenKen, and a whodunit hybrid called <a href="/murdoku/">murder sudoku</a> where you place cat suspects in a mansion and deduce who was alone with the victim. All of it is fully free, playable in the browser with no download and no sign-up, and it comes with levels that ease you in from beginner sizes up. The cat theme is either a dealbreaker or the whole point, depending on your tastes, and we accept that. The puzzles are generated with a guarantee of a unique, logic-only solution, so you never have to guess, and the interface is built to feel calm rather than competitive. If you fall in love with rectangle partitioning, light-up logic, or a bit of mystery on the side, this is a home for it.</p>
